{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.em_coupling_projection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.em_coupling_projection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.em_coupling_projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.em_coupling_projection","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L49-L105","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Setup (commutative ring of coefficients).**\nThroughout, the categorical structure is enriched over the\ncommutative ring\n\n$$\n  R \\;=\\; \\mathbb{Z}\\bigl[q^{\\pm 1/2},\\, (q - q^{-1})^{-1}\\bigr].\n$$\n\nWe **do not** work over $\\mathbb{C}$; every quantity below is defined\nin $R$ and survives any ring map $\\iota \\colon R \\to k$ with $k$ a\ntarget commutative ring (archimedean: $\\mathbb{R}$; $p$-adic:\n$\\mathbb{Q}_p$; finite: $\\mathbb{F}_\\ell$).\n\n**Spectral characterisation.**\nThe electromagnetic fine structure constant is fixed by three\nstructural results that establish both its existence and its\nuniqueness:\n\n1. *Two-strand spectral completeness*\n   ([completeness theorem](#thm\\:em-spectral-completeness)) shows\n   $\\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A \\otimes A)$ has $R$-rank $2$, with\n   exactly two central idempotents $e_+, e_-$ summing to $\\mathrm{id}$.\n   Plancherel completeness $w_+ + w_- = 1$ exhausts the Frobenius\n   mass: **no third channel exists**.\n2. *Uniqueness of the gauge coupling* (corollary, *ibid.*): the\n   singlet idempotent $e_-$ is the unique scalar exchange channel.\n   Any $R$-linear braid-invariant scalar coupling $A \\otimes A \\to\n   \\mathbf{1}$ is a multiple of $\\mathrm{tr}_\\tau(e_-) \\cdot e_-$.\n   So $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{EM}}$ exists, is unique up to global\n   normalisation, and the antisymmetric eigenvalue captures the\n   *entirety* of the EM coupling.\n3. *Force-carrier uniqueness*\n   ([Bring uniqueness](#prop\\:force-carrier-bring-uniqueness)):\n   genus-$4$ torus knots are exhausted by $\\{T_{2,9}, T_{3,5}\\}$\n   alone (a Diophantine fact: $(m-1)(n-1)=8$ with $\\gcd(m,n)=1$,\n   $m \\leq n$ has only the solutions $(2,9)$ and $(3,5)$).  The\n   Bring-supported QOU therefore has a *forced* force-carrier\n   sector with categorical complexity $[9]_q \\cdot [10]_q \\in R$.\n\nThese three results turn $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{EM}}$ from a phenomenological\nfit into a topological invariant of the Bring fibration.  No\ncontour integrals, no factors of $2 \\pi i$, and no renormalisation-group\n\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below splits the manuscript claim into named\n    sub-claim fields; concretisation requires per-block manuscript\n    translation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.claim_iii_bring_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.claim_iii_bring_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (iii) — Bring force-carrier uniqueness:\nthe genus-4 torus knots `T_{m, s}` with `(m−1)(s−1) = 8` are\nexactly `T_{2, 9}` and `T_{3, 5}` (Diophantine fact). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.claim_ii_gauge_coupling_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.claim_ii_gauge_coupling_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (ii) — uniqueness of gauge coupling:\nthere is exactly one singlet (scalar) channel `e_−`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.singlet_channel_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.singlet_channel_count","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Number of singlet (scalar) channels in `End_C(A ⊗ A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.claim_i_two_strand_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.claim_i_two_strand_completeness","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (i) — two-strand spectral completeness:\n`End_C(A ⊗ A)` has `R`-rank 2 with two central idempotents\nsumming to `id_{A⊗A}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.bringTorusKnotCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.bringTorusKnotCount","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The total number of embeddable torus knots `(m, s)` with\n`(m−1)(s−1) = 8`, `gcd(m, s) = 1`, `m ≤ s` —\nmanuscript asserts `= 2` (`T_{2,9}` and `T_{3,5}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.centralIdempotentCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.centralIdempotentCount","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L29-L29","doc":"The number of central idempotents summing to `id_{A⊗A}` —\nmanuscript asserts `= 2` (`e_+`, `e_−`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.endRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.endRank","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The `R`-rank of `End_C(A ⊗ A)` — manuscript asserts `= 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.R","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L24-L24","doc":"The (commutative) coefficient ring `R = ℤ[q^±¹/², (q − q⁻¹)⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.CategoricalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.CategoricalObj","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L22-L22","doc":"Categorical object `A` of the QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjectionContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/em_coupling_projection.lean#L17-L47","doc":"Abstract context for the `em_coupling_projection` claim —\nmanuscript-themed typed fields below; sub-claims encode the three\nstructural inputs that determine `α_EM`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}